WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And one of the
things that the BBC,

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:05.305
the organizer said
at the beginning,

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:09.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that, you know, this
is about saving ourselves,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
our economic models,
because we are, you know,

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.314
most people look
at us and they say,

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.317 align:start size:97% position:3%
"CNN and BBC are
competitors," but we aren't.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:20.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
The real competition
is coming from

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:24.590 align:start size:97% position:3%
these thousands of emerging
alternative media sites

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.662
that are eroding trust
in the legacy sites,

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:34.868
and are taking away
our business model,

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.237
and we need to bond together.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.773
(gentle music)

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.012 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.448 align:start size:84% position:16%
is an environmental
lawyer, author,

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.917 align:start size:97% position:3%
and candidate for president
of the United States,

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.752
Robert F. Kennedy Jr., finally.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.154
Welcome to "the Rubin Report."

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.688
- Dave, thanks for having me.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.824
Sorry it took me so long.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
- (laughing) No, I'm
glad to have you.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.529 align:start size:97% position:3%
And with all the media stuff
you've been going through

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.696
over the last couple weeks,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.464 align:start size:84% position:16%
you've given us
plenty to talk about.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.867 align:start size:97% position:3%
First off, though, you
usually do these interviews

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.268
sitting in your library.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:12.538 align:start size:88% position:13%
Am I getting the special
office interview,

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:13.740
or what's going on here?

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm in a hotel room
at New York City.

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:18.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Hotel in New
York, I'll take it.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.646 align:start size:84% position:16%
All right, so
let's dive into it.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:23.883 align:start size:97% position:3%
I thought before we get
into some of the specifics,

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.685
and all the media stuff
that's been happening

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.722
and everything else,
I was once a Democrat.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when we talk
about you on my show,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
people often ask,
"Dave, what makes RFK

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.363
a Democrat at this point?

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.567
This isn't 1960, 1970, 1980."

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.435
So I guess that's my
first question to you,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.970
what sort of lines you up

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
with the modern Democrat
Party at this point?

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.875
- Well, I don't...

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start size:88% position:13%
My loyalty and
affiliation and affinity

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:59.486
for the Democratic
Party is, you know,

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.987 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the party that
I grew up with.

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:03.922
And I think, you know,

00:02:03.922 --> 00:02:07.259 align:start size:97% position:3%
what's happening in the
party today is unfortunate.

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:09.562
I do think the party,
I do believe the party

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.931
is redeemable, ultimately.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.502
So, and I think our
country's redeemable,

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:20.105
and I think we need both
of those things to happen.

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, if you went
through a checklist, Dave,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:29.082
of all of the things that
my uncle, John Kennedy,

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.050 align:start size:84% position:16%
my father, Robert
Kennedy, believed in,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.919
and Edward Kennedy believed in,

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:37.490 align:start size:97% position:3%
I would kind of check probably
every item on the list.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.296 align:start size:88% position:13%
Whereas today, you
know, some of the issues

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.197
that the Democratic
Party has embraced

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.233
are things that I'm
uncomfortable with,

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think a lot of people
around the country are.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:54.507
And a lot of the traditional
base of the Democratic Party,

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:58.545 align:start size:97% position:3%
which was working people's
unions, American middle class,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:04.684 align:start size:84% position:16%
and now more and
more minorities,
Blacks and Hispanics,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.520
are moving away from
the Democratic Party,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.089
because they feel like
they've been neglected,

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.191
and that the party
is not representing

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.659
(bell dinging)

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:88% position:13%
their interests anymore,
or their values.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.165
- What do you think the best way

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.767
to sort of separate
what I would consider

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.736
the old school classical
liberals, guys like you,

00:03:24.736 --> 00:03:28.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
and your uncle, and your
father, from what's going on

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.611
with the more radical
progressive branch?

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.381
- Well, you know, I just talk,

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:40.453
I try not to talk
about, you know...

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:45.491
I try not to badmouth
anybody, you know.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.561
I think there's been enough
of that in this country,

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.497
and people are done with it,

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:56.302
and we need to find a
path back to civility,

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
and to end this very,
very toxic polarization.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:04.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I try not to, you know,
condemn other people,

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.513 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I just, I talk about the
things that I believe in,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:11.084 align:start position:0%
which are the traditional
values of the Democratic Party.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:15.288 align:start size:84% position:16%
I try to find, and
I've always done this,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
try to identify the values
that we have in common,

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:24.830
rather than focusing on the
issues that hold us apart.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:29.902
You know, I spent
35 years as kind of

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:32.972 align:start position:0%
one of the leading environmental
champions in this country,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.675
but I was speaking regularly,

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:38.077 align:start size:84% position:16%
probably doing 60
big speeches a year,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.879
to mainly Republican groups.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:44.450
And I was getting standing
ovations in most of 'em,

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.353 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I didn't
focus on the issues,

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:50.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
like there's no such thing
as Republican children,

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:53.726
or Democratic children, we
all want a clean environment.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.262
And yet it be had become
a very partisan issue.

00:04:57.262 --> 00:05:00.133
So I tried to talk about
the environment in a way

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know, that every
American could embrace.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:09.642
And I think most of
us, 80% of us agree

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:12.879
on 99% of the issues.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.448
- Yeah, have you been
shocked at the way

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.883
the media's been treating you?

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.317
Because you've been out there,

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:21.454 align:start position:0%
basically talking to everybody,
having open conversations,

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.688 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're talking to
people on the right,

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:24.723
you're talking to
people on the left,

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:28.026
and the media has gone after
you in an absolutely crazy way.

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:30.096
I wanna read one
headline to you,

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.997 align:start size:81% position:19%
it's about your
wife, who I adore,

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:33.966
and we were sort of
in similar circles

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.169
when I lived in L.A.,
and I love "Curb,"

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.470 align:start size:84% position:16%
but this headline
that I'm sure you saw

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.605 align:start size:84% position:16%
from "The New York
Times," "Cheryl Hines,

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
the 'Curb Your
Enthusiasm' actress,

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.743
is beloved in Hollywood.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.312 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now she's supporting the
presidential campaign

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:48.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
of her husband,
Robert F. Kennedy, Jr.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:53.052
Is she normalizing his
often dangerous ideas?"

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.987
I actually retweeted
it, and I asked people

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.956
to come up with some of
your dangerous ideas,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
and nobody seems to
really know what they are,

00:05:59.057 --> 00:06:01.227
but that doesn't stop
"The New York Times."

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.564
- Yeah, and all of my
conspiracy theories,

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.933
as it turns out, have come true.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.434
(Dave laughing)

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.168
They're no longer theories,

00:06:10.168 --> 00:06:13.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're, you know, they're
now proven hypothesis.

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:17.009
But you know what, I
do wonder about it.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.679
I, you know, I was thinking
about this this morning,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:25.685
that because of this,
kind of this hailstorm

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.488
of negative publicity about
me, really kind of nodded,

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.491
it goes beyond like hit pieces

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:34.927 align:start size:88% position:13%
to be just this, you
know, poisonous vitriol.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.298
And that is coming from
all the legacy media,

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:41.701 align:start size:97% position:3%
from "The Atlantic Monthly,"
from "New York Magazine,"

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.003 align:start size:84% position:16%
"New Yorker," from
"The Washington Post,"

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:46.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "The New York Times,"
from "Vanity Fair,"

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:51.944 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Daily Beast," "Daily
Coast," "Rolling Stone,"

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:53.780
and many, many others.

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:57.316
And they all kinda use
the same talking points,

00:06:57.316 --> 00:07:00.753
and they also are not accurate.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:04.557
You know, none of them has
really written an accurate,

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.792 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that's one of the
reasons it doesn't trouble me

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:10.262 align:start size:81% position:19%
is because it's
just inaccuracies,

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:13.166 align:start size:84% position:16%
distortions,
mischaracterizations.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
But one of the things that
kind of occurred to me

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that there's something
bigger at play there

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:24.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
than just their kind
of hatred of me.

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:28.347 align:start size:97% position:3%
That this is, I feel like
I'm kind of on the spear tip

00:07:29.481 --> 00:07:34.353
of a war between this
declining legacy media

00:07:35.487 --> 00:07:39.025
and the evolving and
emerging new media,

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:42.027
the podcasters, the, you know,

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:44.430 align:start size:88% position:13%
all of these
alternative news sites.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.332 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I'm in a
litigation right now

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:48.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
against an organization
called the TNI,

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:52.171
the Trusted News Initiative.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:57.243 align:start size:97% position:3%
The Trusted News
Initiative was a conspiracy

00:07:58.244 --> 00:08:01.279
that was initiated by BBC,

00:08:01.279 --> 00:08:04.216
where they called together
all of the legacy news sites,

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:08.621 align:start size:97% position:3%
including "API," "The
Associated Press," "Reuters,"

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:13.525
the "UPI," "The Washington
Post," and many, many others.

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:17.396
And they married them to
the social media sites,

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:22.468 align:start size:88% position:13%
to Microsoft, to Google,
Facebook, Twitter.

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:26.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they all made an
agreement with each other

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:30.209 align:start size:97% position:3%
that they would censor
certain kinds of information.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:33.245 align:start size:88% position:13%
For example, any
information about COVID

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:36.048 align:start size:88% position:13%
that departed from
government orthodoxies,

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:38.784 align:start size:84% position:16%
but also information
that challenged

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:41.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
any kind of political
orthodoxies,

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:44.490
like any reports on a
Hunter Biden's laptop,

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.192
reports about the Ukraine war

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:51.297
that were inconsistent with
the official U.S. positions.

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:52.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this was an
extraordinary thing,

00:08:52.898 --> 00:08:54.734
this has never happened before.

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:57.770
But we have obtained
during the litigation,

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.973
the internal communications.

00:09:00.973 --> 00:09:03.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
And one of the
things that the BBC,

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:05.945
the organizer said
at the beginning,

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:09.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that, you know, this
is about saving ourselves,

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:13.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
our economic models,
because we are,

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:16.021 align:start size:88% position:13%
you know, most people
look at us and they say,

00:09:16.021 --> 00:09:19.024 align:start size:97% position:3%
"CNN and BBC are
competitors," but we aren't.

00:09:19.024 --> 00:09:20.992 align:start size:84% position:16%
The real competition
is coming from

00:09:20.992 --> 00:09:25.264 align:start size:97% position:3%
these thousands of emerging
alternative media sites

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:30.336
that are eroding trust
in the legacy sites,

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.474
and are taking away
our business model.

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:37.710
And we need to bond together.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.712
And so the way it worked was

00:09:40.779 --> 00:09:42.681
that they would all
identify issues,

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:46.118
and identify individuals
who were saying things

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.153
that should be censored.

00:09:48.153 --> 00:09:52.257
They would notify each
other of those posts,

00:09:52.257 --> 00:09:56.061
or those articles, and
of those individuals,

00:09:56.061 --> 00:09:57.563
they would censor them.

00:09:57.563 --> 00:10:01.334 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then the social media
sites would not allow those,

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:03.102
the sites that printed them on.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:07.706
So if you were, you
know, green med info,

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:08.941
which is, you know,

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:11.644
a site that provides
wellness information,

00:10:11.644 --> 00:10:14.747
or Joe Mercola, or
one of these sites,

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:17.983
these others, Breitbart, or
somebody who was departing

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:20.118
from government orthodoxies,

00:10:20.118 --> 00:10:22.487
you would find yourself
banned on social media.

00:10:22.487 --> 00:10:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
And those sites absolutely
require social media

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:28.961
for their business models.

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:32.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
So if you prevent
them from going viral,

00:10:32.097 --> 00:10:35.835
the way their business model
works is they put in articles,

00:10:35.835 --> 00:10:40.806
they print articles, or publish
articles that then go viral.

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:42.975 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's the only
way that they grow,

00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:44.243
that they earn, you know,

00:10:44.243 --> 00:10:46.445
that they can earn
advertising dollars.

00:10:46.445 --> 00:10:48.314
So if you cut them off there,

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:51.150
and this is what the
memo from BBC said,

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.320
"We need to choke
off those sites."

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.489 align:start size:84% position:16%
So they wanted to
kill all those sites,

00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:59.992 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they did it by agreeing
on a single narrative,

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.527
which was the official
government narrative,

00:11:02.527 --> 00:11:05.831
and then censoring or
ridiculing, you know,

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:09.201
or throttling, or shadow banning

00:11:10.268 --> 00:11:13.339 align:start size:84% position:16%
anybody who challenged
those orthodoxies.

00:11:13.339 --> 00:11:16.242
So you have the, you
know, the legacy media,

00:11:16.242 --> 00:11:19.945 align:start size:84% position:16%
which traditionally
was functioning

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:24.015 align:start size:97% position:3%
as guardians of the First
Amendment of free expression.

00:11:24.015 --> 00:11:27.553 align:start size:97% position:3%
They were, you know, they
were supposed to courageously

00:11:27.553 --> 00:11:31.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
speak truth to power,
maintain this posture of fear

00:11:31.356 --> 00:11:34.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
and skepticism towards
big aggregations of power,

00:11:34.893 --> 00:11:38.030
government corporations, and
they now become the opposite.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:41.434 align:start size:88% position:13%
They become propagandas
for the powerful,

00:11:41.434 --> 00:11:45.071
and oppressors of, you
know, of free speech,

00:11:45.071 --> 00:11:47.506
and the enemies of
the First Amendment.

00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:50.543
And that, you know, I
find myself, you know,

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:55.514
I now see myself as a spear
tip of this emerging media,

00:11:56.782 --> 00:11:59.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is in an
economic competition,

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:02.588 align:start position:0%
but also kind of an ideological,
you know, Armageddon,

00:12:03.388 --> 00:12:05.457
with the old media sites.

00:12:05.457 --> 00:12:09.160
And, you know, so I'm being
championed by Russell Brand,

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:13.465
and by Joe Rogan, and by,
you know, Lex Fridman,

00:12:13.465 --> 00:12:18.504 align:start position:0%
and all of these, you know,
kind of alternative media giants

00:12:20.339 --> 00:12:23.342
in a battle, and I think
they see that as well.

00:12:23.342 --> 00:12:26.912
Russell Brand said
to me something about
that the other day

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:28.948
that sent me thinking, you know,

00:12:30.082 --> 00:12:33.718
about how they need
to, those sites,

00:12:33.718 --> 00:12:36.455
really need to understand
where we all are in this,

00:12:36.455 --> 00:12:39.324 align:start size:84% position:16%
where they are in this
world of, you know,

00:12:39.324 --> 00:12:44.229
of disruption of the
old business model.

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:47.666
- Right, and it's really
bizarre because even now,

00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:50.803 align:start position:0%
when they've been so frequently
exposed for the censorship,

00:12:50.803 --> 00:12:53.405
your interview with my
friend Jordan Peterson,

00:12:53.405 --> 00:12:56.408
from about two weeks ago,
was taken down on YouTube,

00:12:56.408 --> 00:12:58.043
and then they put
it up on Rumble,

00:12:58.043 --> 00:13:00.479
and now you're on Rumble, and
they're not censoring anybody.

00:13:00.479 --> 00:13:02.781 align:start size:97% position:3%
But what do you think
about, so what would you do?

00:13:02.781 --> 00:13:04.950 align:start size:88% position:13%
So if you were president
of the United States,

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.152
what would you do in
terms of big tech?

00:13:07.152 --> 00:13:09.488
Is it breaking them up,
is it regulating them?

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:11.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you connect that
to what you just described

00:13:11.756 --> 00:13:13.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the legacy media,
that's offering, you know,

00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:15.628 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's usually
pushing the pressure

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:16.995
on big tech to do these things?

00:13:16.995 --> 00:13:19.064
And then of course, the
connections we now know

00:13:19.064 --> 00:13:22.000
with the CIA, and FBI,
and everything else?

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.736
- Yeah, well, more
and more, you know,

00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:25.304
we're beginning to understand

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:27.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
this, you know, this
judicial decision

00:13:27.807 --> 00:13:31.643
this week by Judge
Doughty in, you know,

00:13:31.643 --> 00:13:36.715 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the Missouri and Louisiana
Attorney General's cases.

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:42.521
I think really lays it out
that the social media sites

00:13:43.655 --> 00:13:48.494
were kind of victims as
well, of the censorship,

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:51.330
because they were,
and I was, you know,

00:13:53.132 --> 00:13:55.367
the decision is 155 pages,

00:13:55.367 --> 00:13:59.972 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it's a decision that
forbids the Biden White House

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:02.307
from having any contact
with social media sites.

00:14:02.307 --> 00:14:04.442 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's an extraordinary
injunction.

00:14:04.442 --> 00:14:06.811 align:start size:88% position:13%
And it's, yeah, I
think it's bulletproof.

00:14:06.811 --> 00:14:10.983
I think that's why he did this,
you know, 155-page decision,

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:13.852
'cause he wanted to
lay out the evidence.

00:14:13.852 --> 00:14:15.387
And he talks about the history,

00:14:15.387 --> 00:14:19.358 align:start size:88% position:13%
about how the Biden
administration initiated

00:14:19.358 --> 00:14:24.330
this censorship push blitzkrieg.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:30.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I was the first one
that they ordered censored.

00:14:30.902 --> 00:14:33.271 align:start size:97% position:3%
Oh, the Biden administration
came into office

00:14:33.271 --> 00:14:36.408
on January 21st, 2021.

00:14:36.408 --> 00:14:40.679
On January 23rd, they
contacted Facebook,

00:14:40.679 --> 00:14:42.247 align:start size:84% position:16%
the White House
contacted Facebook,

00:14:42.247 --> 00:14:45.350
and asked them to
start to remove me.

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:48.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then three weeks
later there was a battle.

00:14:49.588 --> 00:14:53.225 align:start size:97% position:3%
The people in the White House
were threatening Facebook

00:14:53.225 --> 00:14:57.263 align:start size:88% position:13%
with withdrawal of their
Section 230 immunity,

00:14:57.263 --> 00:15:00.098 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is existential
threat to them.

00:15:00.098 --> 00:15:04.770
Section 230, of course,
is the liability shield.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.773 align:start size:81% position:19%
So that, you know,
if you defamed,

00:15:08.874 --> 00:15:11.376
you know, Donald
Trump on Facebook,

00:15:11.376 --> 00:15:13.112
and said something
that was untrue,

00:15:13.112 --> 00:15:14.613
that you knew to be untrue,

00:15:14.613 --> 00:15:17.483
that was (indistinct)
and very damaging,

00:15:18.584 --> 00:15:21.820 align:start size:84% position:16%
he can sue you, but
he can't sue Facebook.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:25.323
Facebook is supposed to
be a neutral platform,

00:15:25.323 --> 00:15:28.160
and it cannot be sued, and
that's called Section 230.

00:15:29.561 --> 00:15:32.898
Mark Zuckerberg said, "If we
lose that, it's existential,

00:15:32.898 --> 00:15:35.935
we cease to exist," and so-

00:15:35.935 --> 00:15:37.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Right, they would
actually have to censor

00:15:37.369 --> 00:15:39.871 align:start position:0%
more in that case, because
they would have more liability.

00:15:39.871 --> 00:15:42.173
So they'd be basically
censoring everybody.

00:15:42.173 --> 00:15:45.677
- Well yeah, I mean, they
would need to read every,

00:15:45.677 --> 00:15:49.848 align:start position:0%
they would have to have
lawyers read every single post,

00:15:49.848 --> 00:15:52.751
and assess it for, you
know, for defamation.

00:15:52.751 --> 00:15:55.553
There would be no way to do
it, it would just collapse.

00:15:55.553 --> 00:15:59.558 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, and that's what the
White House was threatening,

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:01.659
"If you don't censor these guys,

00:16:01.659 --> 00:16:04.463
we're gonna withdraw your
Section 230 immunity."

00:16:04.463 --> 00:16:07.466 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the White House
was strong arming them

00:16:07.466 --> 00:16:10.168 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the most powerful
way, to censor.

00:16:10.168 --> 00:16:13.605 align:start position:0%
And then the White House invited
in all of these agencies,

00:16:13.605 --> 00:16:16.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
the really weird agencies,
like the Census Bureau,

00:16:16.341 --> 00:16:19.678 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean the CIA was involved,
the FBI was involved,

00:16:19.678 --> 00:16:23.849 align:start position:0%
the DHS, the Department of
Homeland Security was involved,

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:28.586
and also, like the IRS,
and the Census Bureau,

00:16:28.586 --> 00:16:31.456
and a whole bunch of other
agencies were all involved

00:16:31.456 --> 00:16:33.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
in identifying people that
needed to be censored.

00:16:33.791 --> 00:16:36.795 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the things they were
censoring were really crazy.

00:16:38.129 --> 00:16:39.932 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, it was the same
thing that TNI was censoring,

00:16:39.932 --> 00:16:41.332
like Hunter Biden's laptop,

00:16:41.332 --> 00:16:44.002
you weren't allowed
to talk about that.

00:16:44.002 --> 00:16:47.106
Anything to do with the Wuhan
Lab you couldn't talk about.

00:16:48.407 --> 00:16:51.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
But also personal
attacks on the president.

00:16:51.443 --> 00:16:54.213
There was a parody of the
president and his wife,

00:16:55.147 --> 00:16:58.616
that they ordered taken down.

00:16:58.616 --> 00:17:02.554
So this is, you know, really,
this is like King George III,

00:17:02.554 --> 00:17:05.290
you know, back in
the revolution.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.826
This is the reason we had
the revolution was that,

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:10.528
and put the First
Amendment in place,

00:17:10.528 --> 00:17:13.465
so that the king or
the, you know, ruler

00:17:13.465 --> 00:17:15.501
could not silence critics,

00:17:15.501 --> 00:17:17.469 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause if government
can silence his critics,

00:17:17.469 --> 00:17:20.339
it has license for any atrocity.

00:17:21.607 --> 00:17:23.108
- So what would your policy be?

00:17:23.108 --> 00:17:25.143
Would it be that you break
up some of these companies,

00:17:25.143 --> 00:17:27.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
or would it be that
you'd be regulating them,

00:17:27.078 --> 00:17:29.247
or let them collapse?

00:17:29.247 --> 00:17:33.285
- What I, first of
all, on day one,

00:17:33.285 --> 00:17:35.687
I'm gonna issue executive order

00:17:35.687 --> 00:17:40.692
forbidding any federal agency

00:17:43.661 --> 00:17:46.164 align:start size:84% position:16%
from engaging in
censorship activities,

00:17:46.164 --> 00:17:49.535 align:start size:97% position:3%
or recommendations, or
contacts with these companies

00:17:49.535 --> 00:17:52.437 align:start size:84% position:16%
regarding posts that
they don't like.

00:17:52.437 --> 00:17:54.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's, of course, things
that should be removed

00:17:54.839 --> 00:17:59.878
from the internet, you know,
but it's unprotected speech.

00:18:00.946 --> 00:18:06.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, pedophilia,
and you know,

00:18:07.386 --> 00:18:09.988
inciting violence, and you
know, those kinda things

00:18:09.988 --> 00:18:13.758 align:start size:97% position:3%
you can censor without
violating the First Amendment,

00:18:13.758 --> 00:18:15.193
'cause they're not,

00:18:15.193 --> 00:18:16.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're fraudulent.
- Right, they're illegal.

00:18:16.761 --> 00:18:18.263
- Yeah, they're illegal,

00:18:18.263 --> 00:18:20.833
and they're not protected
by the First Amendment.

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:23.268
But otherwise, I'm
gonna order them all,

00:18:23.268 --> 00:18:25.971
not only am I gonna order
them to stop censoring,

00:18:26.972 --> 00:18:30.209 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I'm gonna basically
with, you know,

00:18:30.209 --> 00:18:33.745
reinstate the Smith-Mundt Act,

00:18:33.745 --> 00:18:36.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
which has been effectively
just forgotten about

00:18:36.715 --> 00:18:41.120 align:start size:97% position:3%
and abandoned, that forbids
the federal agencies

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.555
from propagandizing
American people.

00:18:44.756 --> 00:18:47.825 align:start position:0%
And that is just as frightening
what's happening now

00:18:47.825 --> 00:18:50.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the, you know, active
propaganda by the CIA

00:18:50.595 --> 00:18:53.799
through all of these
legitimate media sites

00:18:55.133 --> 00:18:58.737 align:start size:97% position:3%
of our, you know, of debates
about the Ukraine war,

00:18:58.737 --> 00:19:00.271
and about things that Americans

00:19:00.271 --> 00:19:02.307 align:start size:84% position:16%
should not be
propagandized about.

00:19:02.307 --> 00:19:04.976
You know, we should
know who, you know,

00:19:04.976 --> 00:19:07.879 align:start position:0%
I think everybody should be
able to talk about these things,

00:19:07.879 --> 00:19:09.948
but we should know
who it is talking.

00:19:11.082 --> 00:19:13.552
We shouldn't have the
CIA running reporters,

00:19:13.552 --> 00:19:18.624 align:start position:0%
and "Rolling Stone," and
"Daily Kos," and "Daily Beast,"

00:19:19.424 --> 00:19:20.592
and telling us, you know,

00:19:20.592 --> 00:19:22.327 align:start size:88% position:13%
pretending that they're
neutral reporters.

00:19:23.661 --> 00:19:26.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
- How worried are you
that what Trump describes

00:19:26.497 --> 00:19:28.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the swamp, or what
you're, you know, the CIA,

00:19:28.566 --> 00:19:30.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
the three letter
agencies, the deep state,

00:19:30.502 --> 00:19:32.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
all of this stuff,
that going against it,

00:19:32.804 --> 00:19:34.739
and talking about it the
way you talk about it,

00:19:34.739 --> 00:19:36.841
which is somewhat similar to
the way Trump talks about it,

00:19:36.841 --> 00:19:38.944
that it's a machine
that is so embedded,

00:19:38.944 --> 00:19:41.213
or as your uncle
used to talk about,

00:19:41.213 --> 00:19:45.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
that secrecy cannot be a piece
of a flourishing democracy.

00:19:45.016 --> 00:19:47.486
But it's so embedded in
everything right now,

00:19:47.486 --> 00:19:50.022 align:start size:88% position:13%
all of our agencies,
all of our institutions,

00:19:50.022 --> 00:19:51.890
ESG, all of these things,

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:54.125 align:start size:84% position:16%
that it actually can't
change that much.

00:19:54.125 --> 00:19:55.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
It would, you know,
you can go in,

00:19:55.527 --> 00:19:57.595 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you can do executive
actions and all that,

00:19:57.595 --> 00:20:01.900 align:start position:0%
but somehow the system, the
swamp just keeps moving forward.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.502
- Yeah, I don't believe that.

00:20:04.502 --> 00:20:07.105
I, you know, I'm
very excited about

00:20:07.105 --> 00:20:08.739
having an opportunity to fix it.

00:20:08.739 --> 00:20:13.812 align:start position:0%
I've spent, and I think I'm
uniquely positioned to do that,

00:20:15.113 --> 00:20:18.951 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I've spent 40
years suing these agencies,

00:20:20.319 --> 00:20:22.020
and thinking about how do
you unravel agency capture.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.522
And, you know, I've sued,

00:20:24.823 --> 00:20:28.026 align:start position:0%
I've had suits involving almost
all of the major agencies,

00:20:28.026 --> 00:20:33.098
NIH, CDC, FDA, HHS, and then
the Department of Agriculture,

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:40.172
'cause I spent 20 years
suing factory farms,

00:20:40.172 --> 00:20:42.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you know, big
processed food producers.

00:20:42.441 --> 00:20:45.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I saw how that agency
has been taken over

00:20:45.043 --> 00:20:47.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
by industrial
agriculture, and you know,

00:20:47.779 --> 00:20:50.215
has completely drifted
away from its mission

00:20:50.215 --> 00:20:52.384 align:start size:84% position:16%
of protecting small
family farmers,

00:20:52.384 --> 00:20:56.255
and providing America
wholesome food supply.

00:20:56.255 --> 00:20:59.558 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm involved now with
litigation that involves

00:20:59.558 --> 00:21:00.858
the Department of
Transportation,

00:21:00.858 --> 00:21:03.261 align:start size:97% position:3%
on, you know, I'm
representing 1,000 families

00:21:03.261 --> 00:21:06.297
in the Norfolk Southern
spill that, you know,

00:21:06.297 --> 00:21:07.799
upended their lives.

00:21:07.799 --> 00:21:10.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that spill happened
because of agency capture,

00:21:10.302 --> 00:21:12.270 align:start size:88% position:13%
in many of these
agency, I've, you know,

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:17.342
and of course probably 20% of
the 500 environmental cases

00:21:18.676 --> 00:21:23.315 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I've been involved
with have been against EPA.

00:21:24.683 --> 00:21:27.986
You know, which is captured
by the pesticide industry,

00:21:27.986 --> 00:21:33.058
by the oil and coal industry.

00:21:34.192 --> 00:21:38.130
When I sued Monsanto,
we came across emails,

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:40.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
secret emails that
Monsanto had exchanged

00:21:40.998 --> 00:21:42.601
with the head of the
pesticide division,

00:21:42.601 --> 00:21:44.069
a guy called Jess Rowland,

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:46.872
who was taking a
federal paycheck,

00:21:46.872 --> 00:21:48.940 align:start size:84% position:16%
and supposedly working
for the taxpayer,

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:53.912
but secretly he was
working for Monsanto.

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:56.948
And this is the problem,
is that most of the people

00:21:56.948 --> 00:21:59.351
who work at these agencies are
well intentioned individuals.

00:21:59.351 --> 00:22:02.420
They're patriots, they're
good government employees,

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.722
good public servants.

00:22:04.789 --> 00:22:06.691 align:start size:88% position:13%
But the people who tend
to rise to the top,

00:22:06.691 --> 00:22:09.161
and become the division
heads, the branch heads,

00:22:09.928 --> 00:22:11.162
and of course, you know,

00:22:11.162 --> 00:22:13.031
the directors of
those departments

00:22:13.031 --> 00:22:17.569
are people who are in the
tank with the industry.

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:21.072 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they, you
know, set the tone,

00:22:21.072 --> 00:22:24.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they set the
agenda for the whole.

00:22:24.075 --> 00:22:27.846
So I need to go in
there and do that.

00:22:27.846 --> 00:22:31.783
You know, I've spent a lot
of my life studying the CIA,

00:22:31.783 --> 00:22:36.054
because my family's 60-year
fist fight with that agency.

00:22:36.054 --> 00:22:39.558
I know how my uncle was gonna
try to reorganize the agency

00:22:39.558 --> 00:22:41.559
if he hadn't been killed.

00:22:41.559 --> 00:22:44.796
I know exactly what my father
was gonna do with the agency.

00:22:44.796 --> 00:22:46.765
In fact, he had a long
conversation with it

00:22:46.765 --> 00:22:49.568 align:start size:84% position:16%
a week before he died,
with Pete Hamill,

00:22:49.568 --> 00:22:51.203
who's my friend,
who's, you know,

00:22:51.203 --> 00:22:53.171
is a reporter who
was covering him.

00:22:54.373 --> 00:22:56.007 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I don't think it's
a hard thing to do.

00:22:56.007 --> 00:22:58.377
You need to, you know,
you need to get rid of

00:22:58.377 --> 00:23:01.613 align:start size:97% position:3%
the perverse incentives,
these financial entanglements

00:23:01.613 --> 00:23:03.815 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the agencies have
with the industries

00:23:03.815 --> 00:23:05.350
they're supposed to regulate.

00:23:06.417 --> 00:23:08.987
You need to move around
certain individuals,

00:23:08.987 --> 00:23:14.059
and then you need to put
in place really good laws

00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:19.331 align:start size:97% position:3%
against revolving doors,
which is part of the problem.

00:23:20.432 --> 00:23:21.966
You know, people
work for 20 years

00:23:21.966 --> 00:23:25.203
for the federal government
for one of these agencies,

00:23:25.203 --> 00:23:28.607 align:start size:84% position:16%
and as soon as
their pension fast,

00:23:30.008 --> 00:23:32.410
they move over to the industry
that they've been regulating.

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.079
And so they want a good job,

00:23:34.079 --> 00:23:37.449
and a lot of 'em are the
heads of departments now,

00:23:37.449 --> 00:23:39.985 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they end up doing
a bunch of favors

00:23:39.985 --> 00:23:43.121 align:start size:88% position:13%
for these companies
right before they leave.

00:23:43.121 --> 00:23:45.556
And in order to
get the paybacks,

00:23:45.556 --> 00:23:47.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I can give you example
after example of that,

00:23:47.825 --> 00:23:49.227
but we need, you
know, right now,

00:23:49.227 --> 00:23:50.695
they just have to
wait 12 months.

00:23:50.695 --> 00:23:53.365
